  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: Mid-Tech Solution Protected Horticulture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, part of the combi-track Sustainable Horticulture, involves a consortium of eight Dutch and Bangladeshi companies and knowledge institutions working together to enhance sustainable and competitive productivity in Bangladesh&apos;s horticulture sector.Through knowledge exchange and business opportunities, the project aims to improve the sector&apos;s enabling environment. Upon completion, a demonstration greenhouse equipped with mid-tech solutions suitable for local conditions will be established for tomato cultivation. Additionally, hands-on practical training programmes will be conducted in both greenhouse and classroom settings for the benefit of Bangladeshi companies and knowledge institutions.Following the project&apos;s conclusion, new business opportunities for greenhouse establishment will be developed and promoted, sustainable horticultural practices and technologies will be adopted, and new jobs and enterprises will be created.</narrative>
  </description>
